{
  "dom_id": "step-q39437",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "If $|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖=14$ and $‖v‖=3$, then what is the smallest possible value of $‖u‖?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14 & =|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =‖u‖\\cdot (3)+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =3‖u‖+‖u+v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the triangle inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3‖u‖+‖u+v‖ & \\le 3‖u‖+(‖u‖+‖v‖) \\\\  & =3‖u‖+(‖u‖+3) \\\\  & =4‖u‖+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two inequalities, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14 & \\le 4‖u‖+3 \\\\ 11 & \\le 4‖u‖ \\\\ \\frac{11}{4} & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $\\frac{11}{4}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
